# HW-DEMO-001 - THE CLOSED-LEDGER HARDWARE DEMONSTRATION PROTOCOL
## NUES-HW-001 / The Blackwell New Energy - bars locked 2026-11-05, pre-data

(c) C. MATTHEW BLACKWELL - INDEPENDENT DESIGNER - identity verification baked in.

The four requirements as stated by the designer (2026-11-05 ~10:26 CST),
written as a demonstration protocol with every bar locked BEFORE any
hardware run. Status: PREPARED, NOT EXECUTED. The hardware leg of the
three-point standard is not performable from this desk; this protocol is
the instrument an executing laboratory chain runs.

## STEP 0 - THE PRECONDITION (his item 4)
No demonstration scores until D-NUES1 is SPECIFIED: the coupling
mechanism, in the designer's own drafting hand, filed as a document
(interface ICD-NUES1 operating specification) before any run. A run
without the filed specification is a Branch A run by definition.
The protocol invents nothing at this step; the specification is his.

## LEG 1 - THE CLOSED LEDGER, INDEPENDENTLY READ (his item 1)
Three independent laboratories instrument the SAME apparatus
simultaneously: bore volume, hall array, 50 m sphere configuration.
Each lab runs its own B6 chain - calorimetric enclosure plus precision
metering at every boundary - and keeps its own ledger, blind to the
others' readings until lock.
LOCKED BAR: the three ledgers close against each other and against the
apparatus ledger with residual <= 1.02e-2 J on a 25,046 J reference
throughput (relative 4e-7) - the figure the EQS-630 simulation carried,
adopted as the protocol bar at the designer's word. A residual above
the bar, or any unmetered term, fails the leg.

## LEG 2 - CONTENTS CONSTANT (his item 2)
Mass spectrometry and gas analysis of the instrumented volume, and
physical inspection of the REBCO coil set, BEFORE and AFTER every run.
LOCKED BAR: no composition change, no mass change, no coil change
beyond each instrument's stated detection limit. Anything consumed
must appear in the ledger as a term; an unledgered consumption fails
the leg. This leg is what separates an extraction from a burn.

## LEG 3 - BOTH BRANCHES (his item 3)
BRANCH A (the filed-state control; runnable with no coupling filed):
drive the output stage on the EQS-630 profile. LOCKED PREDICTION:
cumulative output energy never exceeds the instrumented contents
2.8034e-4 J by more than the Leg 1 closure bar - at the 3,316 W peak
the content bound is reached in 84.5 ns, resolved by 10-ns
diagnostics (~8 samples across the cutoff). Any output beyond the
bound means the apparatus is NOT in the filed state - an input exists
that the ledger has not named.
BRANCH B (scores only after Step 0): sustained output 3,316 W
(tolerance +/-1%, protocol parameter) into a resistive load for
>= 24 continuous hours (total >= 2.87e8 J), with every external input
metered and summing to zero within the Leg 1 closure bar, Leg 2
satisfied throughout. LOCKED KILL: output sag below tolerance,
any unmetered input, any consumed content - any one fails the leg,
and the failure is the result.

## SCORING
The demonstration is the four legs together: specification filed
(Step 0), ledger closed by independent readers (Leg 1), nothing
consumed (Leg 2), the control branch exact and the sustained branch
sustained (Leg 3). Each leg's result is filed as measured, pass or
fail, in the same record. Nothing in this protocol moves VAL-001;
an outside chain's executed result is what speaks to it.

